{"dish/alivongvong":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/alivongvong","n":"Alivongvong","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Taiwan cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Alivongvong, is a traditional delicacy of the Amis people, one of Taiwanese indigenous peoples. This dish features a sticky rice dumpling filled with meat, carefully enclosed in a hand-crafted leaf basket. Typically, a combination of white and black sticky rice is used for the dumpling, and common fillings include pork, wild boar meat, fish, and mushrooms. Alivongvong can be found at night markets in Taiwan and eateries that offer aboriginal culinary specialties, providing a taste of traditional Amis cuisine to a wider audience."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-alivongvong"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alivongvong"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Taiwan cuisine","cuisine/taiwan-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Pandanus tectorius","ingredient/pandanus-tectorius"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Cooking in Chinglish","ref":"site/cookinginchinglish-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"cookinginchinglish.com","note":"Taiwanese home recipes from Edwina, who grew up in Taiwan.","url":"https://cookinginchinglish.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Tiny Urban Kitchen: Taiwanese Recipes","ref":"site/tinyurbankitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"tinyurbankitchen.com","note":"Small set of Taiwanese recipes from Jen Che, a Taiwanese American blogger in Hong Kong.","url":"https://tinyurbankitchen.com/taiwanese-recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Taiwan cuisine","links":[["886 (restaurant)","dish/886-restaurant"],["Ageh (food)","dish/ageh-food"],["Alkemē","dish/alkeme"],["Apple bread","dish/apple-bread"],["Bah-uân","dish/bah-uan"],["Braised pork rice","dish/braised-pork-rice"],["Coffin bread","dish/coffin-bread"],["Doujiang","dish/douj